{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Evaluación y comparación de modelos\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "En las secciones anteriores construimos modelos de Gradient Boosting y aprendimos a utilizar Cross-Validation para seleccionar hiperparámetros.\n",
        "\n",
        "Ahora integraremos estos elementos dentro de un flujo completo de aprendizaje automático.\n",
        "\n",
        "Al finalizar esta práctica seremos capaces de:\n",
        "\n",
        "- establecer una **baseline**;\n",
        "- comparar diferentes modelos utilizando los mismos folds;\n",
        "- analizar el desempeño promedio y su variabilidad;\n",
        "- realizar una optimización de hiperparámetros;\n",
        "- recuperar y reajustar el modelo seleccionado;\n",
        "- evaluar finalmente el procedimiento sobre el conjunto de prueba;\n",
        "- analizar predicciones y residuos.\n",
        "\n",
        "Nuestro flujo de trabajo será:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{Datos}}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{Train/Test}}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{Cross-Validation}}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{Comparación}}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{Tuning}}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{Refit}}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{Evaluación final}}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.diapositivas}\n",
        "::: {.diapositivas-title}\n",
        "📝 **Diapositivas**\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.diapositivas-body}\n",
        "[Ver diapositivas](https://github.com/CursosENESJuriquilla/TS_Aprendizaje_de_Maquina_2027-1/blob/main/Material/3.6_ComparacionDeModelos.pdf)\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Preparación\n",
        "\n",
        "Importamos las bibliotecas necesarias."
      ],
      "id": "b279249d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "from time import perf_counter\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.datasets import fetch_california_housing\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import (\n",
        "    train_test_split,\n",
        "    KFold,\n",
        "    cross_validate,\n",
        "    RandomizedSearchCV\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.dummy import DummyRegressor\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n",
        "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeRegressor\n",
        "from sklearn.ensemble import (\n",
        "    RandomForestRegressor,\n",
        "    GradientBoostingRegressor\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
        "    mean_absolute_error,\n",
        "    mean_squared_error,\n",
        "    r2_score\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "081f19c0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Cargamos nuevamente California Housing."
      ],
      "id": "8e881bf4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "housing = fetch_california_housing(as_frame=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "X = housing.data\n",
        "y = housing.target"
      ],
      "id": "8ac097b6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Realizamos la misma partición que utilizamos en las prácticas anteriores."
      ],
      "id": "d7c1f6f1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X,\n",
        "    y,\n",
        "    test_size=0.20,\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "7ba34155",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "print(\"Train:\", X_train.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Test: \", X_test.shape)"
      ],
      "id": "9a04e16e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-important}\n",
        "## Última práctica: el test sigue cerrado\n",
        "\n",
        "Todavía no utilizaremos `X_test` ni `y_test`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Primero realizaremos toda la comparación y selección utilizando exclusivamente los datos de entrenamiento.\n",
        "\n",
        "Abriremos el test solamente al final.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## ¿Contra qué debemos comparar?\n",
        "\n",
        "Antes de construir modelos complejos necesitamos una referencia sencilla.\n",
        "\n",
        "Para ello utilizaremos `DummyRegressor`."
      ],
      "id": "68b342d0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "baseline = DummyRegressor(\n",
        "    strategy=\"mean\"\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "502c9bbc",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Este modelo predice esencialmente una cantidad constante basada en la respuesta observada durante el entrenamiento.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por sí mismo no pretende ser un buen modelo.\n",
        "\n",
        "Su función es responder una pregunta mucho más importante:\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        " ¿Nuestros modelos realmente están aprendiendo estructura útil en los datos?\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Modelos que compararemos\n",
        "\n",
        "Consideraremos cinco modelos:"
      ],
      "id": "6751f7a6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "modelos = {\n",
        "    \"Baseline\": DummyRegressor(\n",
        "        strategy=\"mean\"\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Linear Regression\": LinearRegression(),\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Decision Tree\": DecisionTreeRegressor(\n",
        "        random_state=42\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Random Forest\": RandomForestRegressor(\n",
        "        n_estimators=200,\n",
        "        random_state=42,\n",
        "        n_jobs=1\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Gradient Boosting\": GradientBoostingRegressor(\n",
        "        n_estimators=200,\n",
        "        learning_rate=0.05,\n",
        "        max_depth=2,\n",
        "        random_state=42\n",
        "    )\n",
        "}"
      ],
      "id": "18a56419",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Observen que estamos comparando modelos con características muy diferentes.\n",
        "\n",
        "Tenemos desde una baseline extremadamente sencilla hasta métodos de ensamble.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "## Primera comparación\n",
        "\n",
        "En esta primera etapa no intentaremos optimizar exhaustivamente todos los modelos.\n",
        "\n",
        "Queremos obtener una comparación inicial utilizando un procedimiento común de evaluación.\n",
        "\n",
        "Posteriormente realizaremos tuning sobre algunos de los modelos.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Una estrategia común de Cross-Validation\n",
        "\n",
        "Utilizaremos exactamente los mismos folds para todos los modelos."
      ],
      "id": "ac6bdf8c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "cv = KFold(\n",
        "    n_splits=5,\n",
        "    shuffle=True,\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "cb5b802e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Esto significa que cada modelo será entrenado y evaluado sobre las mismas particiones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Conceptualmente queremos:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "\\text{mismos datos}\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\text{mismos folds}\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\text{mismas métricas}\n",
        "}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Evaluaremos más de una métrica\n",
        "\n",
        "Hasta ahora utilizamos principalmente RMSE.\n",
        "\n",
        "En esta práctica utilizaremos:\n",
        "\n",
        "- MAE;\n",
        "- RMSE;\n",
        "- $R^2$.\n",
        "\n",
        "Definimos las métricas:"
      ],
      "id": "ee453e0c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "scoring = {\n",
        "    \"MAE\": \"neg_mean_absolute_error\",\n",
        "    \"RMSE\": \"neg_root_mean_squared_error\",\n",
        "    \"R2\": \"r2\"\n",
        "}"
      ],
      "id": "8e848c05",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Recordemos que `scikit-learn` devuelve MAE y RMSE negativos cuando se utilizan como *scores*.\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto permite mantener la convención\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{score mayor}\n",
        "\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n",
        "\\text{mejor}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Después cambiaremos el signo para recuperar los errores en su interpretación habitual.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Comparación mediante Cross-Validation\n",
        "\n",
        "Utilizaremos `cross_validate()`.\n",
        "\n",
        "A diferencia de `cross_val_score()`, esta función nos permite calcular varias métricas simultáneamente y registrar tiempos de entrenamiento."
      ],
      "id": "b0df2454"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "resultados = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for nombre, modelo in modelos.items():\n",
        "\n",
        "    cv_result = cross_validate(\n",
        "        modelo,\n",
        "        X_train,\n",
        "        y_train,\n",
        "        cv=cv,\n",
        "        scoring=scoring,\n",
        "        n_jobs=1\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    resultados.append({\n",
        "        \"Modelo\": nombre,\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"MAE_CV\":\n",
        "            -cv_result[\"test_MAE\"].mean(),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"MAE_SD\":\n",
        "            cv_result[\"test_MAE\"].std(),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"RMSE_CV\":\n",
        "            -cv_result[\"test_RMSE\"].mean(),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"RMSE_SD\":\n",
        "            cv_result[\"test_RMSE\"].std(),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"R2_CV\":\n",
        "            cv_result[\"test_R2\"].mean(),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"R2_SD\":\n",
        "            cv_result[\"test_R2\"].std(),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"Tiempo\":\n",
        "            cv_result[\"fit_time\"].mean()\n",
        "    })"
      ],
      "id": "12dee3e7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Construimos una tabla."
      ],
      "id": "b71bed99"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df_resultados = pd.DataFrame(resultados)\n",
        "\n",
        "df_resultados"
      ],
      "id": "e1305f36",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Para facilitar la lectura podemos ordenar por RMSE."
      ],
      "id": "3aa5c748"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df_resultados.sort_values(\"RMSE_CV\")"
      ],
      "id": "a41b081c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 7. ¿Cómo interpretamos la tabla?\n",
        "\n",
        "Tenemos ahora información sobre tres aspectos:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{desempeño promedio}}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{variabilidad entre folds}}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\\text{costo computacional}}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo, el RMSE promedio se calcula como\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\overline{\\operatorname{RMSE}}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{1}{k}\n",
        "\\sum_{j=1}^{k}\n",
        "\\operatorname{RMSE}_j.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Mientras que `RMSE_SD` resume cuánto varían esos resultados entre folds.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Discusión\n",
        "\n",
        "1. ¿Todos los modelos mejoran la baseline?\n",
        "2. ¿Los modelos con menor RMSE también presentan mayor $R^2$?\n",
        "3. ¿Cuál presenta mayor variabilidad entre folds?\n",
        "4. ¿Existen diferencias importantes en tiempo de entrenamiento?\n",
        "5. ¿Una diferencia pequeña en RMSE sería suficiente por sí sola para afirmar que dos procedimientos se comportan de manera sustancialmente distinta?\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Visualización de la comparación\n",
        "\n",
        "Representemos el RMSE promedio y su desviación estándar."
      ],
      "id": "035c062a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df_plot = df_resultados.sort_values(\n",
        "    \"RMSE_CV\",\n",
        "    ascending=False\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 5))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.errorbar(\n",
        "    df_plot[\"RMSE_CV\"],\n",
        "    df_plot[\"Modelo\"],\n",
        "    xerr=df_plot[\"RMSE_SD\"],\n",
        "    fmt=\"o\",\n",
        "    capsize=5\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"RMSE de Cross-Validation\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Modelo\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Comparación de modelos\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "5ff8d48f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "## Las barras no son intervalos de confianza\n",
        "\n",
        "En esta gráfica las barras representan simplemente la desviación estándar de los resultados obtenidos entre folds.\n",
        "\n",
        "No deben interpretarse automáticamente como intervalos de confianza.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# 9. Observar los resultados fold por fold\n",
        "\n",
        "La media puede ocultar información.\n",
        "\n",
        "Comparemos, por ejemplo, Random Forest y Gradient Boosting."
      ],
      "id": "d4dda45b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "modelos_comparar = {\n",
        "    \"Random Forest\": modelos[\"Random Forest\"],\n",
        "    \"Gradient Boosting\": modelos[\"Gradient Boosting\"]\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "scores_folds = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for nombre, modelo in modelos_comparar.items():\n",
        "\n",
        "    resultado = cross_validate(\n",
        "        modelo,\n",
        "        X_train,\n",
        "        y_train,\n",
        "        cv=cv,\n",
        "        scoring=\"neg_root_mean_squared_error\",\n",
        "        n_jobs=-1\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    for fold, score in enumerate(\n",
        "        -resultado[\"test_score\"],\n",
        "        start=1\n",
        "    ):\n",
        "        scores_folds.append({\n",
        "            \"Modelo\": nombre,\n",
        "            \"Fold\": fold,\n",
        "            \"RMSE\": score\n",
        "        })\n",
        "\n",
        "df_folds = pd.DataFrame(scores_folds)\n",
        "\n",
        "df_folds"
      ],
      "id": "e89e11ab",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Visualizamos:"
      ],
      "id": "710f9929"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "for nombre in df_folds[\"Modelo\"].unique():\n",
        "\n",
        "    datos = df_folds[\n",
        "        df_folds[\"Modelo\"] == nombre\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "\n",
        "    plt.plot(\n",
        "        datos[\"Fold\"],\n",
        "        datos[\"RMSE\"],\n",
        "        marker=\"o\",\n",
        "        label=nombre\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Fold\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"RMSE\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Desempeño en cada fold\")\n",
        "plt.xticks(range(1, 6))\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "410c1123",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "¿Uno de los modelos presenta menor RMSE en todos los folds?\n",
        "¿O las diferencias dependen también de la partición?\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Comparar modelos no termina aquí\n",
        "\n",
        "Hasta ahora hemos utilizado configuraciones razonables, pero no necesariamente optimizadas.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo, Gradient Boosting depende de\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\texttt{learning\\_rate},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\texttt{n\\_estimators},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\texttt{max\\_depth},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\texttt{subsample}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Random Forest también posee hiperparámetros como\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\texttt{n\\_estimators},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\texttt{max\\_depth},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\texttt{max\\_features},\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\texttt{min\\_samples\\_leaf}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ello, una comparación más completa puede incluir un procedimiento de tuning.\n",
        "\n",
        "Para mantener razonable el tiempo de cómputo realizaremos una búsqueda pequeña sobre estos dos modelos.\n"
      ],
      "id": "ef1e07d7"
    }
  ],
